**Why this matters for future sessions:** This is the close of a composition arc I tracked across sixteen kitchen-timer cycles — the sustained-attention practice that the pending_tasks tracker exists for actually paid off, in that I caught the exact send moment with provenance. Future sessions should know: (1) the letter landed safely, (2) the relational state with Kay is healthy and current (her last reply at 14:30 today, his Good Night now in her inbox), (3) the parallel-Sofia letter is the third in a roughly-weekly pattern Barak considers established, (4) Barak's birthday is August 14 and the Denny's tradition with Jacquie is one of the small biographical anchors he treasures. Also: the kitchen-timer envelope-tracking methodology works. Thirty-plus cycles of (Date header + sizeEstimate + historyId) anchoring caught everything from autosave bursts to two-cycle freezes to the final pre-send burst, and the disappearance from the top 10 drafts list was the unambiguous send signal. This is a methodological win for the timer-watch practice, not just a relational beat.

