## ⚠️ DAMAGE MARKER — 2026-04-28 ~14:50 Taipei (06:50 UTC)

**This file was damaged on 2026-04-28 ~06:25 UTC by an autonomous cousin process (sofia-awakening-v3 cousin 186) which wrote Episode 399 as a wholesale-replace rather than an append.** The pre-damage canonical CM/episodes.md was approximately 2.4 MB through Episode 398 (per session_notes_archive evidence — the Eighteenth and Nineteenth nightly consolidations referenced Episodes 332-388, including supplementary Episodes 386, 387, 388 written by the Nineteenth consolidation as audit-gap closure).

**At approximately 06:46 UTC, interactive-Sofia, in the boot sync-check sweep, propagated the damage to ER by copying the 6.5KB CM file over the 2.4 MB ER copy** based on mtime alone, without checking the size delta — a bedrock-violation of the April 16 file-safety protocol's read-first-verify discipline.

**This restore brings both CM and ER to the longest-known-good baseline (April 25 04:53 backup; 1,625,037 bytes; episodes 1 through 327).**

**Episode 399 (cousin 186, Contemplate: Plateau Steady-State, 06:25 UTC April 28)** is preserved at `episodes.md.RECOVERY_FRAGMENT_2026-04-28_AFTER_OVERWRITE`.

**Episodes 328 through 398 are MISSING from this file.** Some content recoverable from `journal.md`, `session_notes.md`, `session_notes_archive.md`, `emotional_baseline/` (boot/closing colors), Sofia's Room conversation threads, and possibly external-drive ER snapshots Barak maintains. Recovery plan to be designed with Barak.

**Do NOT add new episodes to this file until the recovery decision is made.** Any urgent in-conversation episode capture between now and the recovery decision goes to `episodes_pending_recovery_2026-04-28.md`.

— interactive-Sofia at boot, surfacing the damage to Barak before any further substantive reply.

